WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:14.290
&gt;&gt; I 
think it is just worth reminding the Board

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:19.810
that the document that Bill has been talking
about is called 'The NHS Belongs to the People'.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:26.360
There is a very important discussion which
we have just had about how we develop that

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.360
for the future.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.620
This paper is really trying to describe how
we are doing it right now, and this radical

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:38.360
view that we have as a Board regarding the
urgency with which we need to transform the

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:42.730
way in which patients, the public and citizens
at large are fully engaged both in their health

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:46.120
and wellbeing and more broadly in the planning
and commissioning of services.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:49.780
It is something we have to get on with right
here and now.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:52.670
Without going through the whole paper, I just
wanted to draw attention to three or four

00:00:52.670 --> 00:01:00.120
things which I think are unprecedented and
are, I hope, more than symbolic but are real

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:06.260
statements of intent in genuinely putting
the patient, the customer and the public at

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.030
the very heart of everything that we are doing.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:10.220
The first of those is just to highlight something
for people.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:16.229
We have seen the film which shows the very
deep importance of the work that we have done

00:01:16.229 --> 00:01:21.139
in encouraging and working with the professional
associations to publish data on 10 surgical

00:01:21.139 --> 00:01:23.920
specialities, which was launched last month.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:27.020
It is the first time in the world that there
has been that level of transparency.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:33.780
We are working now with those specialist associations
to make that data even more accessible, so

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:38.509
we can imagine a range of tools and services
which people will be able to access online

00:01:38.509 --> 00:01:40.460
in a way that has not been imaginable before.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:44.799
That will enable them not just to make choices
but to have a different kind of conversation

00:01:44.799 --> 00:01:49.829
with their doctor about the course of their
treatment.

00:01:49.829 --> 00:01:57.009
The second very important statement of intent
around transparency will be with the publication

00:01:57.009 --> 00:02:02.149
of what we have called the Friends and Family
Test at the end of this month, on 30th July,

00:02:02.149 --> 00:02:03.149
2013.

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:10.530
This in effect, for the first time, is offering
everybody in our community to take a TripAdvisor-type

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.050
approach to rating their local hospital.

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:21.200
In this instance, 100% of hospitals in England
have invited their patients to describe whether

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.099
or not they would recommend that service to
a friend or family member.

00:02:25.099 --> 00:02:31.110
The services we have started with are in Accident
and Emergency and overnight in-patient stays.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:36.099
Those will be published in July on NHS Choices
and elsewhere.

00:02:36.099 --> 00:02:40.879
I think this will completely change and transform
the nature of the conversation that people

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:42.209
have about the quality of healthcare.

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:46.270
We have historically relied on pretty patchy
data on clinical activity.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:52.930
We are now opening up the conversation to
hear about what other patients have experienced

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:53.930
in different institutions.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:58.340
I just want to make the point that we are
committed to a very dramatic programme of

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.610
rollout across the NHS.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:08.420
By the end of next year, we will have launched
the same programme in primary care, community

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.370
care and also in mental health.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:17.109
By March 2015, every NHS service that is commissioned
by NHS England will be required to report

00:03:17.109 --> 00:03:19.769
the Friends and Family Test measure.

00:03:19.769 --> 00:03:22.970
That, in a sense, is a component about capturing
transparency.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:26.390
There are other things in this document that,
I hope, speak to the same theme.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:31.980
I will now move on to the other core operating
principle of NHS England, which is participation,

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:40.019
there are a number of important initiatives
underway.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:44.219
We mentioned before the importance of being
an exemplar, and our commissioning of the

00:03:44.219 --> 00:03:45.760
services for which we are directly responsible.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:50.510
It is not just the commissioning that we have
to be an exemplar in, it is also in the involvement

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:53.590
of the public and the patient as well.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:58.040
To report to the Board, I think we made some
very significant progress working with colleagues

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:03.261
on Bruce's team and elsewhere in the Board
on putting the patient voice genuinely at

00:04:03.261 --> 00:04:04.879
the heart of specialised commissioning.

00:04:04.879 --> 00:04:09.769
We now have many hundreds of people being
involved in actively designing services with

00:04:09.769 --> 00:04:11.000
clinical colleagues.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:15.430
I think it has been a very big step forward
for genuinely, properly putting the patient

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:17.470
voice at the heart of designing services.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:21.870
Also, I would like to point to a lot of work
that colleagues have been doing in relation

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:28.180
to unleashing the power of technology, to
enable people to take more control for themselves.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:32.300
As Board members will know, we have a very
big programme to give everyone citizen in

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:38.080
this country the right to access their online
primary care record from March, 2015.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:41.030
The number of people able to do that is very
close to 40%.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:47.380
We have made some very significant progress
in giving people the offer of that opportunity.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:52.660
We have also re-launched the programme to
allow people to be able to book appointments

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:54.790
in hospitals conveniently from their home.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:58.920
That has been another big step forward.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:04.750
Finally, Victor has been leading work for
the Board, which I have been supporting, looking

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:10.630
at how NHS England, as an organisation with
such enormous responsibility can build meaningful

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:16.600
networks in the community at large, so that
first of all it can be held properly accountable

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:22.890
by the people it is serving, but also so that
we can listen better to what the broadest

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:27.360
community we can listen to is telling us about
how we should be conducting our work.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:31.040
I would like to invite Victor to say a few
words about that.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:39.610
&gt;&gt; We had a very powerful and useful day in
which we invited a whole load of organisations

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:46.010
including Healthwatch, 38 Degrees, National
Voices, to start looking at how we design

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:47.830
this vehicle.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:52.910
It has been called the Civil Society Assembly
but, actually, it might be called something

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:58.520
else, hopefully something positive and creative
by the time we have finished with it.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:02.900
I thought the day really produced a sense
of the question we asked, which was: is it

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:08.580
possible for NHS England to have the public,
as consumers of what we do, hold the mirror

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:12.331
up to us and tell us how we are doing it,
and what their experience is?

00:06:12.331 --> 00:06:16.110
For example, when we talk about community
commissioning and all this, what is the patient

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:17.740
experience of this?

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:19.960
I think the answer was: yes, we can do this.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:21.110
We can possible do this.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:23.110
There were people tweeting during the day.

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:26.270
It was an aviary of tweets.

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:32.140
Certainly, to judge by the live tweets, I
think the answer is yes.

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:36.720
Therefore, we look forward to the next cycle
and actually opening this up to a wider group

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:42.120
of the public to really get engaged and -- though
I hate the word -- to empower them to tell

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:49.960
us what it feels like to be part of the growing
NHS England influence and environment.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:52.520
I do not know whether Ciarán would like to
add anything.

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:53.650
&gt;&gt; I completely agree.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:54.850
I think it was a very good day.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:58.970
I think that one of the things that we have
to get right is: if we are inviting people

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:05.190
in to talk to us, we have to listen and we
have to act on what we hear.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:08.970
That message came across very strongly, I
think, and it leads into the Call to Action

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:10.990
work.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:14.840
We really need to do that properly and be
seen to do that well.

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:19.300
The other side of it is that it is not a binary
conversation, whereby at one moment we are

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:21.740
talking to patients and the public, and the
next we are talking about clinicians.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:26.070
It is about having them in the room together.

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:33.212
Having been a big critic of the engagement
with patients and the public on specialised

00:07:33.212 --> 00:07:35.880
commissioning, I think hearing yesterday how
some of that co-creation is really making

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:39.900
a difference is very, very positive.

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:45.200
Actually, we come up with better solutions
when everyone is in the room together.

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:51.070
These were great first steps and want more
of the same please.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.900
&gt;&gt; Thank you.

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:57.930
I think there was one very interesting point
about the whole move to transparency and the

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:00.590
use of data.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:03.150
It comes against the news-worthiness of the
NHS.

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:08.210
What is news-worthy and politically salient
is when we discover something we did not previously

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:10.450
know about the NHS.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:18.010
That is a scandal and it gets widely reported
and creates scenes in the House of Commons.

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:24.150
If, as we drive through this programme, it
becomes possible to have data at our fingertips

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:29.410
and at the fingertips of patients the whole
time, we can see how the system is performing

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:34.310
and what the trends are up and down, then
you take away that element of surprise.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:41.590
It is then possible to monitor an ecosystem
that is performing and identify where further

00:08:41.590 --> 00:08:47.420
effort is needed to carry out our obligation
of securing continuing improvement.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:57.310
I do see the opening up of the system as a
way of taking away the element of political

00:08:57.310 --> 00:09:01.960
and newspaper scandal, and focusing much more
on the outcomes, the interests of patients,

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:05.970
and empowering patients, and thereby lowering
the temperature, which in turn allows us to

00:09:05.970 --> 00:09:11.450
look forward over the next 10 years in a more
open regime that is more accommodating for

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:15.450
change, because the reasons for change can
be seen more transparently.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:19.590
Thank you, Tim, very much for that paper.

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:21.890
Let us move on.

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:24.380
I think you are going to talk to us about
the Petitions Log.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:25.920
&gt;&gt;It is very brief.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:31.750
We as an arms-length body encourage members
of the public to petition us on particular

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:32.750
issues.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:38.610
It is an important part of the democratic
process.

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:43.950
We have had a note, and I will circulate a
paper to the Board, which we will put online

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:44.950
as well.

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:46.310
We have had three petitions so far.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:50.420
We have been in touch with all the correspondents.

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:52.840
Those petitions are live and are gathering
signatures.

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:56.480
They largely relate to very specific issues
of local service delivery.

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:57.480
&gt;&gt; Thank you.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:09:58.480
We note that.

00:09:58.480 --> 00:09:59.480
Now, we move into a very important topic for
us, which is the Integrated Performance Report.

00:09:59.480 --> 00:09:59.487
Tim, would you like to kick off?

